## Review fixes (/projects/sandbox/reviews/pr4297.md)
$ npx jest test/vtid-05309-chat-message-search.test.ts   # 21 passed (deleted-group and strict-cursor tests fail without the fixes)
Fixed: cursor timestamp must be strict ISO (raw microsecond string kept) and is quoted in the filter; the text search is its own query (`content ILIKE`, servable by the trigram index) and file names a second query over attachment/voice rows, merged newest-first; a DM needs a receiver (deleted groups' rows are never "dm:null"); both `filename` and `name` are matched; limiter `validate: { xForwardedForHeader: false }`; paging contract documented in the route header (short/empty pages with a cursor).
Tests added: tenant row check with the tenant filter bypassed, page 2/3 continuity without overlap, full scan window → short page with cursor, type voice/link, `name` match, 429 after 30 searches.
$ (read-only) EXPLAIN of the text query (no trigram index yet)   # Index Scan using idx_chat_messages_user_received (tenant_id) + Filter content ~~* — one tenant holds 52,983 of 53,278 rows, so that index is not selective; the trigram index is what can serve `content ILIKE` there. A staging EXPLAIN with the index can only be shown after RUN-MIGRATION (hypopg is not installed).
Known: PostgREST reads `*` in q as a wildcard; the literal re-check drops the extra rows. The rate limit is per gateway task (in-memory store).
Migration apply target: RUN-MIGRATION applies to Aurora; the counts above come from the Supabase project inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb — confirm pg_trgm there at approval.
